{"id":3895,"date":"2021-10-25T13:53:09","date_gmt":"2021-10-25T20:53:09","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=3895"},"modified":"2025-10-23T13:32:01","modified_gmt":"2025-10-23T20:32:01","slug":"2-6-leds-senior-cde-blockly","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/2-6-leds-senior-cde-blockly\/","title":{"rendered":"2.6: LEDs"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221365870bf\" name=\"6a221365870bf\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>We've Moved!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1761251519553{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-11766\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"81\" height=\"82\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: <a href=\"http:\/\/learn.robolink.com\">Robolink Learn<\/a>! Lessons here will remain available until the end of June 2026. This version of Basecamp will no longer be updated and uses outdated references to Blockly for Robolink. You can access the previous version of <a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/\">Blockly here<\/a>.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221365871f0\" name=\"6a221365871f0\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What is an LED?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>LED<\/strong> stands for \u201clight-emitting diode\u201d. A <\/span><b>diode <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">is an electronic device that allows an electronic current to flow in only one direction. LEDs are beginning to replace traditional light bulbs because they are more efficient.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your CoDrone EDU has 2 <\/span><b>RGB <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">LEDs: one in the center of the drone and one in the remote controller. RGB stands for red, green, and blue. Using the three colors, you can create almost every color imaginable! Aside from making your drone look cool, LEDs provide another form of feedback. For example, the drone light can tell you the connection status of your drone. A solid light means your drone is connected, while a fl<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">ashing light indicates there&#8217;s a disconnection.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22136587272\" name=\"6a22136587272\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Parameters<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CoDrone EDU provides functionality so that you can change the CoDrone EDU&#8217;s LED or the remote controller&#8217;s LED! All<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">of these functions can be found in the &#8220;Lights&#8221; menu.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Each <strong>LED<\/strong> block has the same three components:<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Red, green, blue &#8211; <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">n LED produces a color as a combination of red, green, and blue (hence the name<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">RGB LED). All of these values range from 0 to 255 corresponding to the color&#8217;s intensity, with 255 being the<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">highest. For example, the <\/span>RGB <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">values for the color red correspond to [255,0,0]. <em>What are the RGB values for<\/em><\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em>blue and green? What about purple?<\/em> Use an RGB color picker <a href=\"https:\/\/www.rapidtables.com\/web\/color\/RGB_Color.html\">like <\/a><\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/www.rapidtables.com\/web\/color\/RGB_Color.html\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">this one <\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">to find out!<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Brightness<\/b> &#8211; Determines the brightness of the LED. This can be any number from 0 to 100.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;5628&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221365872d9\" name=\"6a221365872d9\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>LED Rainbow<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Practice using the LEDs to make a rainbow. You will need to research which RGB color value will make each color of the rainbow. <em>For example, how do you make orange from red, green, and blue light?<\/em> Try this code to see what color you see.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10283&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Build a rainbow that cycles through red, orange, yellow, green, blue, purple on the drone. Add a\u00a0<strong>sleep(1)<\/strong> in between each color to see it for 1 second. Set the last parameter of the <strong>set_drone_LED<\/strong> block to 255 for the highest brightness.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10284&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213658733e\" name=\"6a2213658733e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenges<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<b>Challenge: Fading LEDs<\/b><\/p>\n<p>An LED fading in and out can be done by increasing and then decreasing the brightness. In the loops category, use the <strong>count<\/strong>\u00a0block to easily loop through values of 0 to 255.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12642&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]The variable &#8220;i&#8221; can be used to replace the brightness parameter inside the block. The variable &#8220;i&#8221; is automatically generated when you use the\u00a0<strong>count<\/strong>\u00a0block.[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]Hints:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Counting by 1 may be too slow. Try increasing the last parameter.<\/li>\n<li>To count down from 255, one of your parameters has to be a negative number.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22136587397\" name=\"6a22136587397\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Lesson Complete<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>In this lesson, you learned about the CoDrone EDU\u2019s LEDs. You learned how to change the color of the LED using RGB values, and how to combine LEDs with other blocks to make a fading LED.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7547&#8243; img_size=&#8221;750&#215;670&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 7 We've Moved! [vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1761251519553{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}\"] We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: Robolink Learn! Lessons here&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/2-6-leds-senior-cde-blockly\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":4739,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":3877,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1817,1763,1777,1793,626,1533,1438,853,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2108,4328,14401,2120,2122,2126],"class_list":["post-3895","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-cde","lesson-tag-cdej","lesson-tag-led","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-senior","module-intermediate","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3895","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":25,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3895\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13628,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/3895\/revisions\/13628"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/4739"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=3895"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=3895"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=3895"}],"curies":[{"name"